# Docker build context for site/Dockerfile (build context = repo root).
#
# ALLOW-LIST: exclude everything, then re-include only the site code and the
# published hub files. Nothing else in the vault (_meta/, sessions/, practice/,
# work/, softskills/, courses, notes, .git, ...) is sent to the builder.
#
# Rules (Docker: Go filepath.Match plus "**"; patterns are evaluated top to
# bottom and the LAST matching line wins, so re-excludes must come after the
# "!" lines). Spaces inside a pattern are literal and need no escaping.
#
# The two hub lines must stay identical to "include" in site/hubs.config.json
# (site/scripts/test/config.test.mjs checks this). Do not add other "!" lines
# outside site/: that test treats every one of them as a hub glob.
# The real guarantee is site/scripts/verify-context.mjs, which the Dockerfile
# runs on the copied tree; this file keeps the context small and private.

**
!site/**
!technical/*/*/hubs/*-hub.html
!technical/certifications/*/*Study Hub.html

# Re-exclude local dependencies, caches and generated output inside site/.
# The image always builds these fresh.
site/**/node_modules
site/**/.venv
site/**/__pycache__
site/**/*.pyc
site/**/.pytest_cache
site/**/.ruff_cache
site/**/dist
site/build
site/server/public
site/e2e/test-results
site/e2e/playwright-report
site/e2e/blob-report
site/**/*.log

# Never send secrets or OS noise, wherever they are.
**/.env*
**/*firebase-adminsdk*.json
**/*-sa.json
**/service-account*.json
**/.DS_Store
